 </div>
</section>

<section class="page" id="page-experiments">
 <div class="hero"><div class="eyebrow">Experiment operations</div><h2>Configure a reproducible run</h2><p>This control panel is ready to define an experiment. When opened through the local WaveLab server, this panel can launch the training scripts from your project folder.</p><div class="chips"><span class="pill">Configuration builder active</span><span class="pill" id="heroBackendPill" style="color:#ffd39a">Checking backend…</span></div></div>
 <div class="grid two" style="margin-top:14px">
  <div class="card"><div class="section-head"><div><h2>Run configuration</h2><p>Build a JSON configuration for your local project.</p></div></div><div class="control-grid"><div class="field"><label>Dataset</label><select class="select" id="runDataset"><option>Perth 49</option><option>Perth 100</option><option>Sydney 49</option><option>Sydney 100</option></select></div><div class="field"><label>Architecture</label><select class="select" id="runModel"><option>Coordinate MLP</option><option>Spatial-feature MLP</option><option>GNN</option><option>All three models</option></select></div><div class="field"><label>Training seed</label><select class="select" id="runSeed"><option>21</option><option>42</option><option>123</option><option>Custom</option></select></div><div class="field"><label>Custom seed (if selected)</label><input class="textinput" type="number" id="customSeed" value="7" min="0"></div><div class="field"><label>Grouped split seed</label><input class="textinput" type="number" id="splitSeed" value="42"></div><div class="field"><label>Epochs (requested)</label><input class="textinput" type="number" id="epochs" value="100" min="1" max="10000"></div></div><div class="field"><label>Run notes</label><input class="textinput" id="runNotes" placeholder="e.g. sensitivity test on spatial features"></div><div class="note warning">Launch starts the selected Python training script when the dashboard is served by server.py. Keep the terminal open while training runs.</div><div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:14px"><button class="btn primary" id="buildConfig">Build run config</button><button class="btn" id="downloadConfig">Download JSON config</button><button class="btn warn" id="launchRun">▶ Launch experiment</button></div></div>
  <div class="card"><div class="section-head"><div><h2>Execution status</h2><p>Honest runtime state, not simulated training progress.</p></div><span class="pill" id="backendPill">Disconnected</span></div><div class="runstatus" id="runStatus">No run submitted. Configure an experiment and build the JSON payload.</div><div class="progress"><i id="runProgress"></i></div><div class="mini-title">Generated configuration</div><pre id="configPreview" style="white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;color:#a9dfe6;font-size:11px;background:#081624;padding:13px;border-radius:9px;min-height:180px">Click “Build run config” to preview the experiment specification.</pre><button class="btn" id="copyConfig">Copy configuration</button></div>
 </div>
 <div class="card" style="margin-top:14px"><h2>Backend integration contract</h2><p class="muted">The dashboard checks the local service directly. The execution status below reflects the latest response from <code>/api/status</code>. If the service responds but the metric endpoint is unavailable, training status and metrics status may differ.</p><div class="formula">GET /api/status · GET /api/metrics · POST /api/experiments</div><p class="small muted">A successful status check confirms the server is reachable. It does not by itself prove every endpoint is healthy.</p></div>
 <div class="card" style="margin-top:14px"><div class="section-head"><div><h2>Run history</h2><p>Persistent history of dashboard-launched experiments. The original 36 benchmark records remain separately preserved in the research results.</p></div><button class="btn" id="refreshRunHistory">↻ Refresh history</button></div><div id="runHistoryStatus" class="small muted" style="margin-bottom:10px">Loading saved experiment history…</div><div class="tablewrap"><table id="runHistoryTable"><thead><tr><th>Started</th><th>Dataset</th><th>Model(s)</th><th>Seed / split</th><th>Status</th><th>Test MAE</th><th>Test RMSE</th><th>Artifacts</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td colspan="8" class="muted">Loading…</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
</section>

<section class="page" id="page-conclusions">
 <div class="hero"><div class="eyebrow">Current evidence</div><h2>Spatial information improves the surrogate</h2><p>Across the four evaluated datasets, the spatial-feature MLP has the lowest mean test MAE on three datasets. The GNN has the lowest mean test MAE on Perth 100.</p></div>
 <div class="grid two" style="margin-top:14px"><div class="card"><h2>Best mean-MAE model by dataset</h2><div id="winners"></div></div><div class="card"><h2>What we can responsibly claim</h2><div class="phase"><div class="phase-num">✓</div><div><h3>Supported by the current results</h3><p>Spatial features and graph representation improve over the coordinate baseline in mean test MAE for these runs.</p></div></div><div class="phase"><div class="phase-num">!</div><div><h3>Needs further evidence</h3><p>Statistical significance, generalisation to new farms, real-time inference claims, and causal explanations for model differences.</p></div></div><div class="phase"><div class="phase-num">→</div><div><h3>Next research steps</h3><p>Inspect conflicting targets, validate normalization, add prediction-level diagnostics, and test on a strictly held-out layout or external farm dataset.</p></div></div></div></div>
 <div class="card" style="margin-top:14px"><h2>Suggested final-report statement</h2><p id="conclusionText" style="font-size:15px;color:#d4e4f4;line-height:1.8"></p><button class="btn" id="copyConclusion">Copy conclusion</button></div>
</section>
<div class="footer">WaveLab Research Studio · Original seeded benchmark exports are preserved separately from persistent run history · Results are experimental records, not guarantees of future performance.</div>
